# libFuzzer dictionary for the `decode_expr` target.
#
# Every token below was produced by `yesno-wire`'s own encoder, not written by
# hand. Each comes from a minimal well-formed expression -- one per node kind,
# 41 in all -- encoded with `AnyExpr::encode`, decoded back to the same value,
# and also accepted as a pinned `QueryRequest`. Each expression contributes two
# tokens: `<name>_node`, its bytes after the six-byte header, which a mutator
# can splice into a subtree position, and `<name>_whole`, the complete
# encoding.
#
# Why generated: the first version of this file (2026-10-24, 55 tokens) was
# assembled by hand from the tag table, and its fold tokens were `\x07\x00<op>`.
# A fold is the tag, then a whole vector expression, then the operator byte, so
# none of them could parse. View, pack and expand had the same mistake: their
# layout byte comes after a u32 set count, not straight after the tag. Nothing
# reports a dictionary token that cannot parse; the only symptom is a gain that
# is smaller and noisier than it should be.
#
# Measured on 2026-10-24: same minimized starting corpus, 120 seconds per run,
# edges gained per seed:
#
#   no dictionary           6, 8, 8, 11, 16, 9           range   6-16
#   hand-written (55)       76, 90, 14, 30, 37, 42, 48, 66   range  14-90
#   this file (82)          107, 111, 108, 106, 109, 110  range 106-111
#
# The hand-written file's range is the finding: its first two seeds scored
# 76 and 90, and it was adopted on those two; six more put its median near 45.
# The generated file beats every hand-written run and varies by 5 edges.
#
# Pass it explicitly; cargo-fuzz does not pick a dictionary up by name. From
# `yesno-core` the path is `fuzz/decode_expr.dict`:
#
#   cd yesno-core && cargo +nightly fuzz run decode_expr -- -dict=fuzz/decode_expr.dict
#
# A mistyped path is not an error: libFuzzer prints "ParseDictionaryFile: file
# does not exist or is empty" and runs with no dictionary. Check the run log for
# "Dictionary: 82 entries".
#
# To regenerate after a wire-format change, rebuild the token list from minimal
# expressions of every node kind and keep only those that decode back to the
# same value. The generator was a one-off crate and the recipe above is enough
# to rebuild it.

